<div class = "userlogin_container">
<p>Welcome to the help page, here you'll find information on how to use the site.</p>
<p>Storing a username & password: Type a username and password into the form on the main page
   and press register, you'll get a notification stating it has saved successfully and it will
   store it in localstorage where it can be then be used for "logging-in" aka testing it has saved properly.
   Credentials can also be manually added through the given JSON file in the document folder.
</p>
<p>Logging in: Add your username and password to the form on the main page, the program will check
    if your details exist within localstorage or the json, and if successful will "log you in".
    This tool is helpful for confirming your details are saved in the system successfully.
</p>
<p>Finding forgotten credentials: If you somehow have forgotten your already stored login,
   the forgotten username and password pages can help you with this depending on which you've
   lost. Add your known username or password (depending on page) into the box and the
   application will search the localstorage or json for the associated credential, if 
   found it will be displayed saving you the effort of having to remember it.
</p>
<p>Saving credentials in form: If you want to your credentials to be saved in the form, the 
    rememberme checkbox can be used for just that, as long as the checkbox is ticked it will
    keep the details there in the form for further testing later on.
</p>
<p>Password Strength Indicator: This useful tool can be used for testing the strength of your
   password before submitting it to the system, this is very useful in case your unsure the
   password you want to use is all that safe to be using. This indicator checks for upper and 
   lowercase letters, numbers, symbols, etc, to make sure the user is using a wide myriad of
   characters in order for their password to be as secure as possible
</p>
</div>
